                                            <!-- Hidden Full Interview Content -->
                                            <div id="interview-content" class="hidden mt-8 border-t border-gray-200 pt-6 space-y-6">
                                                <div class="space-y-6">
                                                    <div>
                                                        <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">1. What AI innovation or project are you currently most excited about?</h4>
                                                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">I’m most excited about the <b>RFP Gem</b>, which I think most of the legal folks have heard of. After an intensive 6-month journey, we are on the verge of formally piloting and eventually launching it with our sales and proposals teams, and I couldn’t be more excited. I’ve been its champion from day one. The initial spark came from a quarterly sync with Alice, and from there, I’ve had the privilege of leading the charge. Building it from the ground up. It's been a marathon, but I want to be clear that this has been a massive team effort with incredible collaboration and support from all our stakeholders.</p>
                                                    </div>

                                                    <div>
                                                        <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">2. Can you walk us through the problem this AI solution addresses and how it provides value to our team or users?</h4>
                                                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Our current go/no-go process is a manual, multi-stakeholder review that that can consume dozens of man-hours per RFP. It's a non-standardized process that results in subjective, high-variance risk assessment and, critically, yields no analyzable data. Additionally, it is only utilized by one subset of the sales organization, if it’s utilized at all. The <b>RFP Gem</b> is designed to fix this systemically. It leverages a fine-tuned model to perform analysis on complex terms. It parses entire RFP documents and intake forms, extracting and classifying key terms against a predefined matrix of our core legal, security, and business model requirements. It then generates a quantitative risk score and a data-backed 'Go/No-Go' recommendation.</p>
                                                    </div>

                                                    <div>
                                                        <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">3. What was the biggest technical challenge you faced during this project or task?</h4>
                                                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">The real hurdle was translating the deep, human expertise from our internal teams into a language the AI could actually execute reliably. It’s not just about keywords; it’s about concepts. How do you teach an AI to understand the intent behind dozens of different clauses? I quickly learned the AI would sometimes drop instructions or miss a subtle nuance. The solution wasn't a single "fix." It's been countless hours of testing, refining, and collaborating closely with the AI itself and our internal experts to fine-tune the prompts until it was rock-solid.</p>
                                                    </div>

                                                    <div>
                                                        <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">4. In one sentence, how would you describe the impact of this innovation on our team's workflow or future direction?</h4>
                                                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">This gem moves our review process from a manual, subjective bottleneck to a high-speed, data-driven function, instantly aligning Legal, Sales, and Proposals with a single source of truth thus reducing inter-team friction and instead promoting collaboration.</p>
                                                    </div>

                                                    <div>
                                                        <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">5. How do you stay current with the rapidly evolving field of AI?</h4>
                                                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">You can't just be a spectator in this field. Besides reading articles and talking with colleagues, I believe you have to be hands-on. I'm constantly experimenting. I’m testing new tools, pushing prompts to see where they break, and even revisiting old prompts to see how the underlying models have improved. The field is moving too fast for just theory; you have to "live it" through daily trial and error.</p>
                                                    </div>

                                                    <div>
                                                        <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">6. What is your personal philosophy on the role of AI in our industry?</h4>
                                                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">I’ll be the first to admit I was an AI skeptic. I had the same "will it replace me?" anxiety many people feel. My entire mindset shifted during Paul’s prompting seminar at the legal team offsite, where I had an "a-ha!" moment: AI isn't a replacement; it's an <b>amplifier</b>. My philosophy now is that AI is a powerful tool in our toolkit. It's not a cure-all, and it absolutely requires human oversight. It’s here to handle the repetitive work, which frees us up to focus on the critical work that requires deep human expertise and strategic nuance. What excites me most is watching AI become more concept-aware. It’s already moving beyond simple keyword matching to understand meaning, like knowing "indemnify without limitation" is the concept of "<b>uncapped liability</b>." As that capability grows, it will build incredible trust between users and AI, and unlock entirely new ways for us to work smarter.</p>
                                                    </div>

                                                    <div>
                                                        <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">7. Is there a tool, library, or technique you've recently adopted that has fundamentally changed the way you approach your work?</h4>
                                                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">I’ve most recently adopted the <b>Improve Prompt</b> feature in Harvey. This feature utilizes AI before the response generation. Good input is one of, if not the most, important components of AI use. The improve prompt feature works to make your prompt clearer, more thorough, and more AI friendly. The best part is, it can be applied to any AI platform. I will go into Harvey, pop in my prompt, and use the improve prompt feature. I think rework the prompt and bring it over to Gemini if I’m not if I think that’s the more appropriate platform for the project/task. This has allowed for exponentially better input on my end, meaning better base output and less reworking to try and get the AI to understand what I am asking it.</p>
                                                    </div>
